This file contains the tables used in the statistical analysis for the LTMLE football project.

Table 1 defines the variables used in the longitudinal model, including baseline variables, time-varying covariates, treatment variables, and the outcome.

Table 2 describes the treatment trajectories (abar values), which represent patterns of performance over time.

Table 3 presents the results of the LTMLE analysis, including additive treatment effects (ATE), relative risk (RR), odds ratios (OR), and p-values for both minimal and maximal models.

These tables provide a structured summary of the dataset and the results used in the final report.


# Tables

## Table 1. Variable Definitions Used in Our Analysis

| Component | Description | Variable Name |
|----------|------------|--------------|
| W | Baseline variable, remains constant over time | Years_Played_Before_t1 |
| L1 | Time-varying covariates at t1 | Passing stats (attempts, completions, touchdowns, interceptions) |
| A1 | Treatment at t1 | Yards_Category_t1 |
| L2 | Time-varying covariates at t2 | Passing stats |
| A2 | Treatment at t2 | Yards_Category_t2 |
| Y | Outcome variable | Played_in_t3 |

---

## Table 2. Treatment Trajectories (abar Values)

| Trajectory | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| (0,0) | Low performance at t1 and t2 |
| (0,1) | Low to high performance (improvement from t1 to t2) |
| (1,0) | High to low performance (decline from t1 to t2) |
| (1,1) | High performance at t1 and t2 |

